Z||000011||Wannabe||11-14-2001||08:38 PM||||Yes, the GTZ wheels are 16x7. A refreshing anomoly in the GM lineup. The 45mm offset makes them a particularly good fit tfor the '88s as well.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Wade87GT||11-14-2001||10:38 PM||||MR2KLR,  I'm looking at a spare wheel right now. Molded, on the backside of the "spokes" is, "MADE IN U.S.A", "10097504", "16 X 7 X 42.0", "WWH", AND "MOLD 4". Other than some more pictures (I'll e-mail them to you when I find them or take some more) that should be more than enough info that you can use. Except, if you're going to strip and repaint, that's a PITA job. I used four 1 quart cans of the nastiest stripper and still haven't gotten all of the old paint off. My local bead/sand blasters wanted $75. per wheel. I know, some of ya'll have your own super-garage...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
